<section class="bear-list">

    <!-- BROWN BEAR -->
    <div class="bear-item">
        <img src="images/brown.jpg" alt="Brown Bear Habitat">
        <h3>Brown Bear</h3>

        <p>
            Brown bears are one of the most widespread bear species in the world, found across North America, Europe, and Asia.
            They inhabit forests, mountains, and tundra regions. Their diet changes depending on the season and location.
            In spring and summer they eat berries, roots, insects, and plants, while in autumn they consume large amounts of fish
            such as salmon to prepare for winter hibernation.
        </p>

        <p>
            They are highly adaptable omnivores and can survive in many different environments. Their strong foraging skills
            and ability to adjust their diet make them one of the most successful large mammals on Earth.
        </p>

        <iframe class="bear-map"
            src="https://www.google.com/maps?q=Alaska+forest&output=embed"
            style="border:0; margin-top:15px; border-radius:10px;"
            loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>

    <!-- POLAR BEAR -->
    <div class="bear-item">
        <img src="images/polar.jpg" alt="Polar Bear Habitat">
        <h3>Polar Bear</h3>

        <p>
            Polar bears live in the Arctic region and are perfectly adapted to life on sea ice.
            They depend on frozen oceans to hunt seals, which are their primary food source.
            They travel long distances across ice sheets in search of breathing holes and hunting areas.
        </p>

        <p>
            Polar bears are almost entirely carnivorous, and their survival is directly linked to sea ice conditions.
            Climate change and melting ice are major threats to their habitat and population.
        </p>

        <iframe class="bear-map"
            src="https://www.google.com/maps?q=Arctic&output=embed"
            style="border:0; margin-top:15px; border-radius:10px;"
            loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>

    <!-- GIANT PANDA -->
    <div class="bear-item">
        <img src="images/panda.jpg" alt="Giant Panda Habitat">
        <h3>Giant Panda</h3>

        <p>
            Giant pandas live in the mountain forests of central China, mainly in regions covered with dense bamboo.
            Their habitat is cool and humid, which supports bamboo growth, their main food source.
        </p>

        <p>
            Although they belong to the carnivore family, pandas eat almost exclusively bamboo.
            They spend most of their day feeding because bamboo is low in nutrients and difficult to digest.
        </p>

        <iframe class="bear-map"
            src="https://www.google.com/maps?q=Sichuan+China+bamboo+forest&output=embed"
            style="border:0; margin-top:15px; border-radius:10px;"
            loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>

    <!-- BLACK BEAR -->
    <div class="bear-item">
        <img src="images/black.jpg" alt="American Black Bear Habitat">
        <h3>American Black Bear</h3>

        <p>
            American black bears live in forests across North America, including mountains, swamps, and wooded valleys.
            They are highly adaptable and can live near human settlements.
        </p>

        <p>
            Their diet includes fruits, nuts, insects, fish, and small mammals.
            They are opportunistic feeders and will eat almost anything available in their environment.
        </p>

        <iframe class="bear-map"
            src="https://www.google.com/maps?q=North+American+forest&output=embed"
            style="border:0; margin-top:15px; border-radius:10px;"
            loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>

    <!-- SLOTH BEAR -->
    <div class="bear-item">
        <img src="images/sloth.jpg" alt="Sloth Bear Habitat">
        <h3>Sloth Bear</h3>

        <p>
            Sloth bears are native to India and Sri Lanka, living in tropical forests and grasslands.
            They prefer warm climates with dense vegetation and abundant insect populations.
        </p>

        <p>
            Their diet mainly consists of termites and ants, which they extract using their long snouts.
            They also eat fruits, honey, and sometimes small animals.
        </p>

        <iframe class="bear-map"
            src="https://www.google.com/maps?q=India+wildlife+forest&output=embed"
            style="border:0; margin-top:15px; border-radius:10px;"
            loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>

    <!-- SUN BEAR -->
    <div class="bear-item">
        <img src="images/sun.jpg" alt="Sun Bear Habitat">
        <h3>Sun Bear</h3>

        <p>
            Sun bears live in the tropical rainforests of Southeast Asia, including Borneo and Malaysia.
            They spend much of their time in trees, where they build nests and search for food.
        </p>

        <p>
            Their diet includes fruits, insects, honey, and small animals.
            They are excellent climbers and very secretive, making them difficult to study in the wild.
        </p>

        <iframe class="bear-map"
            src="https://www.google.com/maps?q=Borneo+rainforest&output=embed"
            style="border:0; margin-top:15px; border-radius:10px;"
            loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>

